## Summary
Yes. sv and guesses are needed (8/10 and 7/10 mice by > 10 held-out NLL); leak and urgency are not (summed −21 / +26;
only PSUIM6 benefits). Part of the leak/urgency gain seen on all trials (PSUIM5, PSUIM7) came from pulse trials.

## Summary
**PASS on all six items. No issue changes D's reported numbers.**
- I recomputed with my own dict/loop code from the frozen trial table. It reproduces every checked per-mouse value and group value in D's `contrast_table.csv` to within 3e-13 pp. That covers:
  - positive − negative Δdirection at onset + 4.58 s, both summaries;
  - pulse vs control in both directions;
  - the three-arm common effect;
  - one pseudo-onset seed.
- Running my estimator at the absolute 5 s deadline reproduces package C exactly. So the D-vs-C differences come only from the horizon (onset + 4.58 s versus 5 s) and from onset eligibility.
- Minor items only (ISSUE-minor): the identity check is weak as evidence, and `curves.csv.gz` has no interval-method column. Neither changes any number.
